{"text": "feasible", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Anglo-Norman <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">fesable</i>, from Latin <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">facere</i>, Old French <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">fesable, faisable</i> (\u201cdoable\u201d), from <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">fere, faire</i> (\u201cto do\u201d) + <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">-able</i>.\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Adjective", "definitions": [{"definition": "Able to be done in practice.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {"Synonyms": ["achievable", "doable", "possible", "practicable", "workable"], "Antonyms": ["infeasible", "unfeasible"]}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["General American", "/\u02c8fi.z\u0259.b\u0259l/"], ["Received Pronunciation", "/\u02c8fi\u02d0.z\u0259.b\u0259l/"], ["General Australian", "/\u02c8fi\u02d0.z\u0259.b\u0259l/"]]}